msgid "Public members"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:26
msgid ""
"Whether this pipe is suitable for handle passing between processes. Only "
"a connected pipe that will be passing the handles should have this flag "
"set, not the listening pipe that uv_accept is called on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:30
msgid "The :c:type:`uv_stream_t` members also apply."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:34
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:38
msgid ""
"Initialize a pipe handle. The `ipc` argument is a boolean to indicate if "
"this pipe will be used for handle passing between processes (which may "
"change the bytes on the wire). Only a connected pipe that will be passing"
" the handles should have this flag set, not the listening pipe that "
"uv_accept is called on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:46
msgid "Open an existing file descriptor or HANDLE as a pipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:48
msgid "the file descriptor is set to non-blocking mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:51
msgid ""
"The passed file descriptor or HANDLE is not checked for its type, but "
"it's required that it represents a valid pipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:56 ../../src/pipe.rst:69
msgid "Bind the pipe to a file path (Unix) or a name (Windows)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:58
msgid ""
"Does not support Linux abstract namespace sockets, unlike "
":c:func:`uv_pipe_bind2`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:61
msgid "Alias for ``uv_pipe_bind2(handle, name, strlen(name), 0)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:64 ../../src/pipe.rst:94
msgid ""
"Paths on Unix get truncated to ``sizeof(sockaddr_un.sun_path)`` bytes, "
"typically between 92 and 108 bytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:71
msgid ""
"``flags`` must be zero or ``UV_PIPE_NO_TRUNCATE``. Returns ``UV_EINVAL`` "
"for unsupported flags without performing the bind operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:74 ../../src/pipe.rst:104
msgid ""
"Supports Linux abstract namespace sockets. ``namelen`` must include the "
"leading nul byte but not the trailing nul byte."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:80 ../../src/pipe.rst:110
msgid ""
"Paths on Unix get truncated to ``sizeof(sockaddr_un.sun_path)`` bytes, "
"typically between 92 and 108 bytes, unless the ``UV_PIPE_NO_TRUNCATE`` "
"flag is specified, in which case an ``UV_EINVAL`` error is returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:86 ../../src/pipe.rst:99
msgid "Connect to the Unix domain socket or the Windows named pipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:88
msgid ""
"Does not support Linux abstract namespace sockets, unlike "
":c:func:`uv_pipe_connect2`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:91
msgid "Alias for ``uv_pipe_connect2(req, handle, name, strlen(name), 0, cb)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:101
msgid ""
"``flags`` must be zero or ``UV_PIPE_NO_TRUNCATE``. Returns ``UV_EINVAL`` "
"for unsupported flags without performing the connect operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:116
msgid "Get the name of the Unix domain socket or the named pipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:118 ../../src/pipe.rst:135
msgid ""
"A preallocated buffer must be provided. The size parameter holds the "
"length of the buffer and it's set to the number of bytes written to the "
"buffer on output. If the buffer is not big enough ``UV_ENOBUFS`` will be "
"returned and len will contain the required size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:123
msgid ""
"UNIX domain socket paths on FreeBSD cannot exceed the size of "
"``sockaddr_un.sun_path`` although the platform defines a "
"``SOCK_MAXADDRLEN`` that is larger."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:127
msgid ""
"the returned length no longer includes the terminating null byte, and the"
" buffer is not null terminated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:132
msgid ""
"Get the name of the Unix domain socket or the named pipe to which the "
"handle is connected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:144
msgid ""
"Set the number of pending pipe instance handles when the pipe server is "
"waiting for connections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:148
msgid "This setting applies to Windows only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:153
msgid "Used to receive handles over IPC pipes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:155
msgid ""
"First - call :c:func:`uv_pipe_pending_count`, if it's > 0 then initialize"
" a handle of the given `type`, returned by :c:func:`uv_pipe_pending_type`"
" and call ``uv_accept(pipe, handle)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:159
msgid "The :c:type:`uv_stream_t` API functions also apply."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:163
msgid ""
"Alters pipe permissions, allowing it to be accessed from processes run by"
" different users. Makes the pipe writable or readable by all users. Mode "
"can be ``UV_WRITABLE``, ``UV_READABLE`` or ``UV_WRITABLE | UV_READABLE``."
" This function is blocking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:172
msgid ""
"Create a pair of connected pipe handles. Data may be written to `fds[1]` "
"and read from `fds[0]`. The resulting handles can be passed to "
"`uv_pipe_open`, used with `uv_spawn`, or for any other purpose."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:177
msgid "Valid values for `flags` are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:179
msgid ""
"UV_NONBLOCK_PIPE: Opens the specified socket handle for `OVERLAPPED` or "
"`FIONBIO`/`O_NONBLOCK` I/O usage. This is recommended for handles that "
"will be used by libuv, and not usually recommended otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/pipe.rst:184
msgid "Equivalent to :man:`pipe(2)` with the `O_CLOEXEC` flag set."
msgstr ""

